    "## 5. What to look for\n",
    "\n",
    "* **Step 0 vs step 1.** The first frame is pure noise by construction. Whether the second frame\n",
    "  already carries visible structure says how much of the solution is decided by the very first\n",
    "  gradient rather than accumulated over the epoch.\n",
    "* **Where the gradient lives.** The gradient panels are the informative ones at init: they show\n",
    "  *which cells* the loss is pushing on before the parameters have moved. Compare the layer-2\n",
    "  gradient's active region against where the construction's non-zeros sit (own token x key\n",
    "  predecessor, `[0:8, 108:116]`).\n",
    "* **Gradient vs applied step.** In section 2, $\\|g\\|$ and $\\|\\Delta W\\|$ are on the same axes.\n",
    "  Adam divides by a running RMS, and in the first few steps that RMS estimate is still warming\n",
    "  up, so the early steps are unusually large relative to their gradient.\n",
    "* **Epoch boundaries.** The dotted lines mark step 98/196/... If the batch loss visibly steps\n",
    "  down at a boundary rather than sliding, the model is fitting the epoch's shuffle rather than\n",
    "  the task.\n",
    "* **Layer 1 vs layer 2.** The norm panel puts all four curves together. In the epoch-level run\n",
    "  layer 1 outgrows layer 2 despite a much smaller gradient; this window shows when that starts.\n"
